  "dom_id": "step-q67004",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The geometric series $2+10+50+250$ can be written using sigma notation as",
  "worked_solution": "We must express the given series in the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ denotes the first term of the series, $r$ denotes the common ratio, and $N$ denotes the number of terms in the series. In this case, ${a}_{1}=2$ and $N=4.$\n\nTo find $r,$ we calculate the ratio of the first two terms in the series:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{10}{2}=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, expressing the geometric series given in sigma notation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+10+50+250 & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{4}2\\cdot {5}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
